      ],
      "extract": "Systems of algebraic equations can be encoded geometrically in an algebraic variety. This apparently harmless observation is the starting point for the development of such a successful branch of modern Mathematics as Algebraic Geometry. One of the leading principles behind most of the mathematical work of Alexandre M. Vinogradov is that Partial Differential Equations (PDEs) should be treated in a similar way.",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
