        {
          "term": "diffiety",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "\\label{Sec:Geom} In this section we show that a system of, generically non-linear, PDEs can be encoded into a geometric object: a \\emph{diffiety}. We will work in the rather general setting of a PDEs imposed on submanifolds $N$ of a fixed dimension $n$ in a manifold $P$ (see \\cite{klv86}), in contrast with most of the literature where only PDEs imposed on sections of a fibration (or a fiber bundle) are considered.",
      "extractCut": false
    },
